<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A user image with a text or icon fallback when it's missing.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/avatar)

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Avatar do
  AvatarImage(src: "/avatars/01.jpg", alt: "Sarah Jenkins")
  AvatarFallback { "SJ" }
end
```

Avatar represents a person or entity. Compose it from its parts:

- **Avatar** - the root that sets size and shape and clips its children to the rounded silhouette.
- **AvatarImage** - the photo. It stays hidden until it has loaded, so a broken or slow image never
  flashes; the `ui--avatar` controller then swaps it in for the fallback.
- **AvatarFallback** - what shows until (or unless) the image loads: initials or an icon.
- **AvatarBadge** - an optional status dot in the corner.
- **AvatarGroup** - a wrapper that overlaps a row of avatars and passes a shared size/shape down.

The whole component is sized in em, so a single `size:` (a preset or a pixel number) scales the
image, fallback text, and status badge together.

## Examples

### Fallback

When the image is missing, still loading, or fails to load, `AvatarFallback` renders instead. Use
initials for people, or an icon for a generic placeholder.

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :fallback %>

```ruby
Avatar(size: :lg) do
  AvatarImage(src: user.avatar_url, alt: user.name)
  AvatarFallback { user.initials }
end

Avatar(size: :lg) do
  AvatarFallback { Icon(:user_filled) }
end
```

### Sizes

Seven presets run from `:"2xs"` to `:"2xl"`. Because the avatar is sized in em, the fallback text
and status badge scale along with the image.

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :sizes %>

### Custom size

Pass a number to `size:` for an exact pixel dimension when a preset doesn't fit. It drives the
root's font-size, so everything inside still scales proportionally.

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :custom_size %>

```ruby
Avatar(size: 44) { ... }
```

### Shape

`shape: :circle` (the default) renders a full circle; `shape: :rounded` uses a squircle-style
rounded square for a more app-like look.

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :shape %>

### Status badge

Drop an `AvatarBadge` inside the avatar for a corner status dot. Add `animate: true` for a pulsing
ping that draws the eye to an online indicator, and recolor it with a `text-*` class.

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :status_badge %>

```ruby
Avatar(size: :lg) do
  AvatarImage(src: user.avatar_url, alt: user.name)
  AvatarFallback { user.initials }
  AvatarBadge(animate: user.online?, class: ("text-foreground-subtle" unless user.online?))
end
```

### Avatar group

`AvatarGroup` overlaps a row of avatars and rings each one with the background color so they read
as a stack. It passes a shared `size:`/`shape:` to its children, and any non-image avatar (like a
+5 counter) sits in the same rhythm. `orientation: :vertical` stacks them in a column.

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :group %>

```ruby
AvatarGroup(size: :md, aria_label: "Project members") do
  members.first(4).each do |member|
    Avatar do
      AvatarImage(src: member.avatar_url, alt: member.name)
      AvatarFallback { member.initials }
    end
  end
  Avatar { AvatarFallback(class: "text-foreground-muted text-sm") { "+#{members.size - 4}" } }
end
```

### Loading animation

`AvatarFallback` renders until the image finishes loading, so a pulsing placeholder inside it is
swapped for the photo automatically - no extra state needed. The demo image is served with a 2.5s
delay; use the embed's reload to watch it again.

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :loading %>

```ruby
Avatar(size: :xl, class: "bg-transparent") do
  AvatarImage(src: user.avatar_url, alt: user.name)
  AvatarFallback { span(class: "bg-background-strong size-full animate-pulse rounded-[inherit]") }
end
```

### Listening for loading changes

The controller moves the root's `data-status` through `idle`, `loading`, `loaded` and `error`, and
dispatches `ui--avatar:loading-status-change` with `{ status }` (React's `onLoadingStatusChange`).

```ruby
Avatar(data: { action: "ui--avatar:loading-status-change->profile#avatarStatus" }) { ... }
```

### RTL

The status badge moves to the start corner and the group stacks from the right, because both are
expressed with logical properties.

<%= embed UI::AvatarPreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Avatar

The root. Renders a `<span>` that sizes and clips its children.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `size:` | `:"2xs"`, `:xs`, `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg`, `:xl`, `:"2xl"`, `Integer` | `:md` | A preset scale, or a pixel number for an exact size. |
| `shape:` | `:circle`, `:rounded` | `:circle` | Full circle or rounded square. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. |

### AvatarImage

The photo. Renders an `<img>` that is shown once the source has loaded.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `src:` | `String` | - | Image URL. Without one the avatar stays on its fallback. |
| `alt:` | `String` | `""` | Alternative text describing the person or entity. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. |

Other attributes (`loading: "lazy"`, `srcset:`, …) go on the `<img>`.

### AvatarFallback

Shown until (or unless) the image loads. Renders a `<span>`.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `delay:` | `Integer` | - | Milliseconds to wait before showing the fallback (avoids a flash on fast loads). |
| block | | - | Initials or an icon. Text renders at 0.4em; an svg fills the avatar. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. |

### AvatarBadge

An optional status dot in the corner. Renders a `<span>`.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `animate:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Add a pulsing ping behind the dot (skipped under reduced motion). |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes - recolor with a `text-*` class. |

### AvatarGroup

Overlaps a row of avatars and passes a shared size/shape down. Renders a `<div>`.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `size:` | Avatar `size:` | - | Default size for child avatars that don't set their own. |
| `shape:` | Avatar `shape:` | - | Default shape for child avatars that don't set their own. |
| `orientation:` | `:horizontal`, `:vertical` | `:horizontal` | Stack the avatars in a row or a column. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. |

A child Avatar's own `size:`/`shape:` always wins over the group default.

## Accessibility

- Give every meaningful `AvatarImage` an `alt:` that names the person or entity. For a purely
  decorative avatar, leave `alt: ""` (the default).
- The `AvatarFallback` text (initials) is visible content, so it's announced; for an icon-only
  fallback, the icon is decorative - make sure the surrounding context names the user.
- `AvatarBadge` is a visual status indicator. If the status matters, say it in text nearby
  (e.g. "Online") rather than relying on the dot's color alone.
- In an `AvatarGroup`, each avatar keeps its own accessible name; add an `aria_label:` to the group
  (e.g. "Project members") and visible text for any +N overflow count.
- The badge's pulsing animation is skipped when the user prefers reduced motion.
